pool.baseline:
system prompt: You are a senior DevOps engineer specializing in AWS infrastructure.

I'm working on a deployment where a Lambda function needs to write logs to an S3 bucket, but I'm hitting an "Access Denied" error. I've reviewed my IAM policy and the bucket policy, and they seem to align, but the service still can't get through. 

Here is the current IAM policy attached to the Lambda role:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:PutObjectAcl"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::prod-logs-storage-99/*"
    }
  ]
}

I've confirmed the ARN matches the bucket exactly. Can you review this and tell me why the access is being blocked?

